// Title: Potential NTLM Coercion Via Certutil.EXE
// Sigma ID: 6c6d9280-e6d0-4b9d-80ac-254701b64916
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-01 | Modified: 2023-02-14
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects possible NTLM coercion via certutil using the 'syncwithWU' flag
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/issues/243
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_certutil_ntlm_coercion.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\certutil.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "CertUtil.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -syncwithWU " and ProcessCommandLine contains " \\\\")
